fastdoku
========

Portions of this software are derived from tdoku, a fast Sudoku solver by
Tom Dillon:

    tdoku
    https://github.com/t-dillon/tdoku
    Copyright (c) 2019, Tom Dillon
    BSD 2-Clause License

Credit for the DPLL + triad + SIMD architecture -- the box-as-4x4-matrix
state with negative triad literals, the band-as-configurations
representation, the elimination-message tables, and the branching heuristic
-- belongs to Tom Dillon. This project ports that design and benchmarks
against it.

Derived files
-------------

  src/triad.rs
      A Rust port of tdoku's src/solver_dpll_triad_simd.cc. The architecture,
      lookup tables, and update rules follow that file closely.

  bench/tdoku_fastpath.cc
      A modified copy of tdoku's src/solver_dpll_triad_simd.cc, used only by
      the benchmark harness. The sole modification is the hot/cold split of
      BoxRestrict and BandEliminate (marked "FASTPATH EXPERIMENT" in the
      file), which is not the work of tdoku's author. It exists so the
      benchmark can measure that one optimization in isolation.

Both files carry the upstream copyright notice and BSD 2-Clause terms.

