Other acknowledged designs
--------------------------

  src/jcz.rs
      An original implementation of the JCZSolve architecture -- bands
      stored by digit with locked-candidate propagation through small
      lookup tables -- as published on the enjoysudoku forum by
      zhouyundong_2012, with refinements by champagne and JasonLion. No
      existing implementation's code was used: the file is written from the
      algorithm's published description, and its tables are derived from
      first principles (and verified exhaustively in its tests). The
      algorithmic credit belongs to those authors.

Other data
----------

The benchmark corpora used in the README's measurements belong to the tdoku
repository and are NOT redistributed here; clone tdoku and unzip its
data.zip to reproduce those numbers.

data/top95.txt and data/hardest11.txt are Peter Norvig's published hard-puzzle
lists (https://norvig.com/sudoku.html). data/gen500.txt and data/gen5000.txt
were generated by this project's own `fastdoku gen`.
